Care and Supportive Care Group The Cochrane Library</source><year>2003</year><comment>Update Software</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gysels</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Higginson</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving supportive and palliative care for adults with cancer: research evidence manual</article-title><source>[Web document]</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London: National Institute for Clinical Excellence</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nice.org.uk/pdf/csgspresearchevidence.pdf"/><comment>[cited 22 September 2006]</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Scottish Intercollegiate Guidelines Network</collab></person-group><article-title>Guideline 75 &#x02013; Supporting material: epithelial ovarian cancer</article-title><source>[Web document]</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Edinburgh: SIGN</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.sign.ac.uk/guidelines/published/support/guideline75/searchnarrative.html"/><comment>[rev. 8 Mar 2005; cited 22 September 2006]</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eagar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An Australian casemix classification for palliative care: lessons and policy implications of a national study</article-title><source>Palliat Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>233</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15198135</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1191/0269216304pm876oa</pub-id></citation></ref><ref i